        "id": 265467,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2026-05-14T18:31:59.264Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yeah, I wasn’t aware of it. I suspected it when Adam started doing more game streaming during business hours, and taking commissions, but I assumed GtG was just keeping him on payroll as a sort of reverse honorarium.</p>\n<p>It’s also worth noting that GtG does not currently control <a href=\"http://greaterthangames.com\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">greaterthangames.com</a> (this website), and now live at <a href=\"https://greaterthan.games\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://greaterthan.games</a>, which doesn’t have a forum yet. The implication is that GtG will get this site back at some point, but can’t right now for legal reasons. Which is really odd to me—typically if you have a website that you don’t have the trademark for, the trademark owners can petition the registrar to transfer it, and potentially sue for it. But the registry expires 2026-10-06T18:50:53Z, so I’d guess that GtG can claim it then.</p>",
