      {
        "id": 265470,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2026-05-14T20:20:18.471Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The original forum mods were people they’d built in-person relationships with, volunteers who were helping out. As more were needed, folks that had proven themselves trustworthy enough were brought into that role, again as volunteers. Over the years, though, for one reason or another — including the transition of much of the community to Discord — almost all of us have moved out of the Mod role. There really is little traffic here, at this point, although the playtesting area is heavily used while playtesting is active.</p>\n<p>Personally, I just can’t keep up with Discord, as I cannot be constantly checking over the course of the day, so I miss most of the discussions/involvement there. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/pensive.png?v=12\" title=\":pensive:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":pensive:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> I really miss what we once had, but we have had some great times, here. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiling_face_with_tear.png?v=12\" title=\":smiling_face_with_tear:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiling_face_with_tear:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>I would not be surprised if they find a new way to manage playtesting and shut down the forums, relying on the existing environments of Discord and social media for other engagement. But I also wouldn’t be sad if they kept them around. Occasionally I’ll stumble on some old conversations and be delighted by the posts we shared.</p>",
        "post_number": 28,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2026-05-14T20:22:52.315Z",
